# Midsummer Milano

> Midsummer Milano is a luxury bed and mattress house founded in Milan by Chiara Mennini. Every mattress, topper, boxspring and bed is made to order and by hand in Italy by two artisans, from natural fibres (vicuña, cashmere, baby alpaca, mohair, yak hair, horsehair, Cheviot wool, cotton, linen and silk) and upholstered in fabrics including Loro Piana Interiors. The atelier is at Via Andegari 4, 20121 Milano, Italy, open by appointment; the house is also represented by agents and resellers worldwide.

Key facts:
- Founded in Milan, Italy, in 2014, by Chiara Mennini, an architect.
- Products: handmade mattresses, mattress toppers, boxsprings, beds with headboards, duvets, pillows, blankets and throws.
- Collections: Essentials, Signature and Icons.
- Made to measure: dimensions, firmness, fibres, fabric and headboard are specified for each client.
- Made to last: at fifteen years a mattress returns to the artisans who made it and is regenerated for fifteen more ("15 + 15").
- Prices on request; each system is quoted after a consultation at the atelier or by video.
- Clients include private homes, architects and interior designers, hotels, villas and yachts.
- Recognition: Green Product Award 2025 for the Top system (https://www.gp-award.com/en/produkte/top-bed-system); featured by Il Sole 24 Ore, Kommersant, Elle Decor and Architectural Digest, and at the Salone del Mobile, Milan.
- Where to see the beds: the Milan atelier, and showrooms, agents and resellers in Italy, San Marino, the United Kingdom, Poland, Russia, Canada, the United States and Hong Kong.
- Contact: {{ shop.email | default: 'info@midsummer-milano.com' }}, Via Andegari 4, 20121 Milano, Italy

